  "minimal_new_parser_rules": [
    "Explicit named OPEN request ID and explicit new application PID; never guess latest.",
    "Match exact bare OPEN timing and validated host wire/control request. Ignore timestamp-prefixed NSLog duplicate. Require exactly one accepted named callback, same boot/timebase, request ticks preceding new main; no overlapping competing OPEN.",
    "Select one complete five-hook sequence for selected new PID, seq1..5, exact hook set, nondecreasing ticks and paired validated relay provenance; retain old incarnation separately rather than modifying first-launch/warm parser strictness.",
    "Require new PID differs from selected prior PID and new main tick differs/increases. With original query_result56 and nonzero uniqueid, require distinct kernel incarnation identifiers and no identity rejection. If unavailable, label PID/main-tick-only scope and do not invent unique IDs.",
    "Require prior old-PID lifecycle or timing evidence and a completed ps table: matched BEGIN/END nominal label, one exact header, all nonblank table lines parse to PID/PPID/UID/STAT/COMM, no duplicate PIDs, status0 and timed_out0. Unrecognized/interleaved partial rows make absence inconclusive.",
    "Require no old PID row AND no exact owned executable path row in selected table. Explicit host read/snapshot of this completed table must precede OPEN command creation/transmission. Retain observed timestamp, serial prefix length/hash and byte offsets. END before callback log alone cannot prove absence preceded the actual request.",
    "New active lifecycle starts generation0 and shares new PID/main tick/timebase; pair original process identity and original lifecycle provenance.",
    "Derive request-to-main, main-to-appeared/active, request-to-callback/active in exact rational nanoseconds. Keep host absence ordering separate from guest interval clock.",
    "Root separately reviews ordinary AppSwitcher dismissal, Home, newly returned app and counter state. Process absence alone does not establish cause of termination.",
    "Call outcome process launch after observed absence, never cold/cleared-cache launch or native-device performance. Preserve existing warm parser behavior and narrow original-SMC prefix rule."
  ],
  "limits": "Boot37 windows demonstrate exact readable format and old process presence, not old-process absence or a fresh-process trial. No live VM input, new permissions or process termination used."
